      <div class="stage" data-reveal>
        <div class="stage-marker"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-home"/></svg></div>
        <div class="stage-head">
          <div class="stage-title">Home → BLR T2</div>
          <span class="stage-when">Mon Jul 13 · 02:30 dep · 03:30 arrival</span>
        </div>
        <div data-route="car"
          data-from="HOME" data-from-label="Bangalore" data-from-time="Mon · 02:30"
          data-to="BLR" data-to-label="BLR T2" data-to-time="Mon · 03:30"
          data-duration="1h · ~40 km"></div>
        <p style="font-size: 14px; color: rgba(246, 241, 232, 0.85);">Pre-book Uber Reserve <strong style="color: var(--saffron-soft);">48h prior</strong>. Family of 4 + 4 large suitcases needs Uber XL or Ola Prime SUV. Reach BLR T2 by 03:30 for a 06:00 international departure — at least 3h before takeoff.</p>
        <div class="stage-body">
          <div class="stage-col">
            <h6>Check before leaving</h6>
            <ul>
              <li>Passports for all 4 with eVisa printed (validity 6+ months)</li>
              <li>Hotel + flight + Klook + Shinkansen confirmations on phone + 1 printed copy</li>
              <li>Web check-in done T-1 day · seat selection confirmed</li>
              <li>Wallet · ₹15K cash · ¥30K (or forex card pre-loaded) · cards activated for international use</li>
              <li>Power: phones + power banks ≤27000mAh in carry-on, USB-C cables, Japan-compatible adapters (Type A — same as US, no adapter needed for two-pin)</li>
              <li>Travel insurance papers · pediatric script copies</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="stage-col">
            <h6>Carry vs check</h6>
            <ul>
              <li>Carry-on: docs, electronics, ORS, kid snacks, change of clothes for 6yo</li>
              <li>Checked: bulk clothes, toiletries, gifts, summer light layers (Tokyo Jul = 30°C+)</li>
              <li>Each adult 23kg + each kid 23kg = 92kg checked allowance (Malaysia Airlines economy)</li>
              <li>Liquids ≤100ml each in transparent pouch (carry-on rule, applied at KUL too)</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="link-chips">
